   "source": [
    "# Which features relate to the target (daily_revenue)?\n",
    "feats = ['temperature_c','iced_drink_sales','hot_drink_sales','cold_brew_sales',\n",
    "         'salad_sales','foot_traffic','barista_shoe_size','pastry_demand']\n",
    "cafe[feats + ['daily_revenue']].corr()['daily_revenue'].sort_values(ascending=False)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "427888a1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "`foot_traffic` (≈ 0.72) and `iced_drink_sales` (≈ 0.68) are the strongest positive predictors, `hot_drink_sales`\n",
    "(≈ −0.51) is a strong *negative* predictor (still useful — the sign just tells the direction), and\n",
    "`barista_shoe_size` (≈ 0.00) carries no information.\n",
    "\n",
    "Now a redundancy check between two features:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "344db4d4",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-22T08:16:04.082951Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-10-22T08:16:04.082562Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-10-22T08:16:04.088389Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-10-22T08:16:04.087224Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
